KILLED   stall threshold ignores the aircraft data: 1 failing checks (e.g. the stall threshold comes from the aircraft data)
KILLED   no minimum stall duration: 1 failing checks (e.g. a brief α spike is not a stall)
KILLED   spin never detected: 1 failing checks (e.g. a stall with sustained yaw rate is a spin)
KILLED   bank change from the first stalled sample: 1 failing checks (e.g. a stall with a large bank change is a tip stall)
KILLED   dive judged on the final path only: 2 failing checks (e.g. a pull-out that starts too late is still a dive  Hard landing: landing gear collapsed sink 9.0 m/s, 32.0 m/s)
KILLED   gear collapse checked before flight conditions: 3 failing checks (e.g. gear overtravel at the end of a dive is still a dive)
KILLED   dead stick on any engine stop: 1 failing checks (e.g. an engine that just stopped is not yet a dead stick)
KILLED   director records no history: 2 failing checks (e.g. real stall flight is explained as a stall  Crash no flight history)
KILLED   card omits the cause: 1 failing checks (e.g. the crash card shows the cause)
